<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Panel A shows ultrasound images of hearts in stages of contraction and expansion, some with red segmentation and some without. Panel B displays a histogram of video count versus ejection fraction percentage, highlighting the normal and abnormal videos selected for the study. Panel C presents a series of ultrasound images with segmentations of varying opacities from 100% to 0% in 20% increments.) /K 670 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 60 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
631 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (A pigeon is inside an operant conditioning chamber, interacting with a screen displaying an exemplar flanked by two report buttons. The setup includes equipment connected to the chamber. On the right, four panels labeled 1 to 4 depict different stages of a typical training trial in the experiment: a white star representing the start stimulus, a segmented exemplar, that same exemplar flanked by two report buttons, and the word "Feedback" indicating the outcome of pecking one of the report buttons.) /K 671 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 63 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
632 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graph showing proportion correct over 50-trial blocks for segmented \(blue\) and nonsegmented \(orange\) groups. Each group has normal \(solid circle\) and abnormal \(open circle\) categories. Proportion correct increases across trial blocks, with segmented group performing better overall. Error bars indicate within-subject variability.) /K 672 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 63 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
633 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar chart showing the proportion correct by video type, with error bars. Segmented Training has the highest proportion at about 0.83, followed by Novel Nonsegmented at approximately 0.75, and Familiar Nonsegmented is lowest at about 0.67. A dashed line marks the 0.5 level.) /K 673 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 64 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
634 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar graph comparing the proportion correct for "Non-learners" and "Learners" across three video types: Nonsegmented Training, Familiar Segmented, and Novel Segmented. "Learners show a decrement in performance from Nonsegmented Training videos to Familiar Segmented and Novel Segmented videos. Non-learners show an improvement in performance from Nonsegmented Training videos to Novel Segmented videos. Error bars indicate within-subject variability.) /K 674 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 65 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
635 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graph showing pigeons proportion correct over six 700-trial blocks for normal and abnormal categories. Normal category \(solid line\) displays an upward trend, beginning around 0.55 and reaching 0.75. Abnormal category \(dotted line\) starts at 0.50, also trending upward to approximately 0.70. Error bars indicate variability.) /K 675 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 65 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
636 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar chart comparing the proportion correct for two video types, Segmented Training and Novel Segmented, across two categories, Normal and Abnormal. Normal scores are higher than Abnormal for both types. Error bars indicate variability.) /K 676 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 66 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
637 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar graph comparing accuracy between normal and abnormal categories across two video types: Segmented Training and Familiar Nonsegmented. For Familiar Nonsegmented videos, performance is substantially above chance for the Normal category and substantially below chance for the Abnormal category, suggesting a response bias for those videos.) /K 677 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 66 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
638 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graph showing the number of sessions versus opacity percentages for four subjects. Each subject is represented by different symbols: squares for Subject 14W and 44W, and circles for Subject 76B and 29B. The number of sessions sharply increases at the last opacity each subject was exposed to.) /K 678 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 67 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
639 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graphs show the proportion correct during daily sessions at the last opacity 55 sessions for four subjects labeled 14W \(0 percent\), 44W \(10 percent\), 76B \(20 percent\), and 29B \(40 percent\). Each plot displays fluctuations that are predominantly below a dashed line marking 0.7 proportion correct.) /K 679 0 R /P 507 0 R /Pg 68 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
